      "specialAbilities": [
        {
          "name": "Crush",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "A sand worm can roll over onto opponents as a standard action, using its whole body to crush them. Crush attacks are effective only against Medium or smaller opponents. A crush attack affects as many creatures as can fit under the sand worm's body. Creatures in the affected area must succeed on a Reflex save (DC 27) or be pinned, automatically taking 10d4+18 points of bludgeoning damage during the next round unless the sand worm moves off them. If the sand worm chooses to maintain the pin, treat it as a normal grapple attack. Pinned opponents take damage from the crush each round if they don't escape. The save DC is Constitution-based.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Earthquake",
          "type": "su",
          "description": "A sand worm can cause the ground to erupt around it within a 30-ft.-radius. Creatures within the area of effect take 8d6 points of earth damage and are inflicted with the Weighted status effect. A successful Reflex save (DC 21) reduces the damage by half and negates the status effect). Blue mages may learn this ability as a 4th level spell (Knowledge: Arcana DC 23).",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "A huge, powerful, hundred-foot-long worm burrows through the sands looking for its next meal. The worm's thick, segmented hide ranges in color from tan to golden brown, providing natural camouflage."
